    "description": "LTP Padded Frame (Canik TP9): Laffs Dynamics\n\nVariant of the Uberclay's Bozkurt pistol frame, a 3DP version of the Canik TP9 pistol. Mostly aesthetic changes. \n\n*Added material to the picatinny rail.\n*Squared off the front of the pic rail.\n*Scalloped the pic rail slots.\n*Elongated the trigger guard by 6mm. (Squeeze in some gloved fingies)\n*Added aesthetic \"padding\" on the front and sides of the grip section.\n*Added semi-wrapped ridging along the bottom half of the backstap.\n*Added material to the rear of the frame. \n\nOverall, this was more for my own purposes, but I decided to release this in case any weirdo wanted a similar look from the base frame.\n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 218C\nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16mm\nWall Perimeters: 8+ \nInfill: 90%+\nInfill Pattern: Gyroid\nSupport Material Percentage: 18%\n\n\n\nNotes: \n\nThis file pack is for the frame only. Other printed part files will need to be downloaded from the base design release; link provided in the below text.\n\n\n\nBase Bozkurt pistol frame files can be found on Odysee: \n\nOdysee: https://odysee.com/@TheGatalog-PrintableFramesReceivers:9/The-Bozkurt-Canik-TP9:c\n\n(Other print settings and the hardware list will be provided in the base data pack)\n\n\n\nAccreditations:\n\nUberclay: Creator of the Bozkurt pistol frame; used the base frame model from their design release.",
